<title>CHINA: China Liaoning province '96 grain output seen up.</title>
<headline>China Liaoning province '96 grain output seen up.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's northeastern Liaoning province expects a harvest of 32 million tonnes in 1996, a rise of four million tonnes from 1995 despite serious flooding in the past two years, the Xinhua news agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>The province has pumped 1.58 billion yuan into agriculture so far in 1996, a rise of 20 percent compared with the year-ago period, it said. That included 500 million yuan for repairing farmland and agricultural facilities damaged by floods.</p>
